{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:5254-1","published":"2026-11-16T13:30:27Z","modified":"2026-11-17T17:23:14.186923808Z","related":["CVE-2024-14029","CVE-2026-103261","CVE-2026-103262","CVE-2026-103263","CVE-2026-115927","CVE-2026-116577","CVE-2026-116578"],"upstream":["CVE-2024-14029","CVE-2026-103261","CVE-2026-103262","CVE-2026-103263","CVE-2026-115927","CVE-2026-116577","CVE-2026-116578"],"summary":"Security update for python-tornado6","details":"This update for python-tornado6 fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2024-14029: duplicate `Transfer-Encoding: chunked` headers are ignored, which allows for HTTP request smuggling\n  (bsc#1284796).\n- CVE-2026-103261: failure to limit the number of query string fields in `HTTPServerRequest.__init__` allows remote\n  attackers to cause event-loop stalling (bsc#1283943).\n- CVE-2026-103262: unbounded memory accumulation in `CurlAsyncHTTPClient` allows remote attackers to cause denial of\n  service (bsc#1283961).\n- CVE-2026-103263: `StaticFileHandler` follows symbolic links outside the static root and allows unauthorized users to\n  gain read access to sensitive files (bsc#1283974).\n- CVE-2026-115927: event loop blocking and excess memory use from chunked bodies with many small chunks allows for\n  denial of service (bsc#1289051).\n- CVE-2026-116577: quadratic CPU usage when parsing HTTP headers with line folding allows for denial of service\n  (bsc#1289066).\n- CVE-2026-116578: open redirect via crafted request paths in `RedirectHandler` URL templates allows for phishing\n  attacks (bsc#1289059).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"python-tornado6","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Module for Python 3 15 SP7","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/python-tornado6&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Module%20for%20Python%203%2015%20SP7"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"6.3.2-150400.9.32.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"python311-tornado6":"6.3.2-150400.9.32.1"}]},"database_specific